* Norns, grendels and ettins sleep when sleepy (openc2e Creatures 2 project, our
* own scripts). Run by openc2e after the world loads (Additions folder);
* safe to repeat.
*
* C2's sleep script (4 0 0 41) lets a creature sleep only while its
* Tiredness (drive 5) is above 48, and rest when tired but not sleepy.
* Sleepiness (drive 6) rises in the dark and falls only while asleep (the
* sleep stimulus, 22). In C2's own grendel genome walking tires a grendel
* only once it is old, so grendels, and the Home ettin, sat at Sleepiness
* 255 and could never sleep. The owner asked (2026-11-10) to replace that
* rule for grendels and ettins (norns keep C2's): a grendel or ettin with
* Sleepiness above 96 sleeps, however rested, until Sleepiness is below 10;
* one only tired (Tiredness above 48) lies down to rest.
*
* Norns too (owner, 2026-11-12): in Home's logs most norns sat at the mind's
* sleepiness cap (about 70% of their decisions) and rarely slept, being
* sleepy but not tired. C2's norn script also dreams after sleeping (DREA,
* which works C2's own brain); our creatures run their own mind, so that
* part is left out.
* Rest goes on until Tiredness is below 16 (2026-11-22; before, below 48, the
* level it starts at, so a tired creature lay down, got up and lay down again
* every few seconds), or half a minute, as it does not help every genome.
* any world: it changes objects by kind, not Eden's map, so it runs on every
* world (other Additions run only on worlds started from Eden.sfc).
*
* Dropping off where they stand (2026-11-22; owner's screencast: creatures
* asleep through the day, on and on, even at 8.5x). A very sleepy body's own
* reflex, C2's event 69 (Sleepiness over 230), lays it down for about 40 s
* with only two sleep stimuli (22), so Sleepiness hardly fell: it woke, still
* at 200-255, dropped off again within 3 s, and so on for good, a starving
* one too (its hunger cannot keep an exhausted creature awake). In a copy of
* the owner's world, 675 of 894 sleeps ended at that 40 s mark, 737 with
* Sleepiness over 150. The reflex now sleeps as event 41 does: a stimulus
* every 27 ticks until Sleepiness is below 10, or about five minutes; the
* mind still wakes it for a pressing need (wakeReason).
*
* Both sleep scripts give the sleep stimulus every 27 ticks (as before),
* until Sleepiness is below 10, or at most 120 times (about five minutes).
* (2026-11-22: creatures at the incubator slept nearly all the time; the
* cause was the waterfall by its pond, script-patches.txt (it calms only, now). Stimulating sleep
* every 8 or 15 ticks was tried: creatures slept 5% or 9% of the time, 11%
* at 27, so the game's own pace stays.)
scrp 4 2 0 41
  doif driv 6 gt 96
    impt 15 pose 58 aslp 1
    setv var1 0
    loop
      impt 15 wait 27 stm# writ targ 22
      addv var1 1
      doif driv 6 lt 10 setv var1 120 endi
    untl var1 ge 120
    impt 1 wait 20
    aslp 0
  else
    doif driv 5 gt 48
      setv var0 0
      loop
        impt 5 pose 58 wait 20 stm# writ targ 21 addv var0 1
        doif driv 5 lt 16 setv var0 15 endi
      untl var0 ge 15
    endi
  endi
endm
